# The lockfile IS committed for this project, against the repo-wide rule in the
# root .gitignore (20 Sep 2026). Not a preference: npm 10 cannot build this
# dependency tree from package.json alone. It dies with "Cannot read properties
# of null (reading 'edgesOut')" partway through vitest's peer set, which is an
# arborist bug rather than anything wrong here, and it happens on a CI runner and
# on a laptop alike. So without this file there is no install, and without an
# install there is no CI. It also makes every install reproducible, which is what
# a check is supposed to be.
!package-lock.json
